From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: on-device render fixes, deploy.py, OHOS patches

Fixes found bringing the shim up on an rk3568 (M1 render):
- start the servo thread in LibraryLoaded (CreateNWeb can precede
  InitializeWebEngine)
- set opts.config_dir from --user-data-dir (the OHOS font cache unwraps it)
- buffer the initial load until the browsing context is registered
- defer WebView creation until the first real Resize, and set the OHNativeWindow
  buffer geometry before creating the surfman surface (otherwise WebRender OOMs
  into ACE's 1x1/producer surface)
- let WebView::resize own the rendering-context resize. Resizing the context
  directly first makes Painter::resize_rendering_context early-return (it is
  already at the target size), which skips the WebRender document-view update,
  the display-list resend and set_needs_repaint -- no new frame is scheduled and
  the old one persists until an unrelated event (a tap) forces a repaint. Most
  visible as a half-height page after the soft keyboard closes, once the IME is
  wired. Buffer geometry is still set first, before the surfman resize that
  resize() performs. With the context no longer held for that direct resize,
  BuiltWebView does not keep one: the painter and the delegate hold their own.

Add tools/deploy.py (hdc-py based) and ohos-patches/ (the OpenHarmony webview
diff plus apply/build instructions) for reproducibility.

Validation: Test by deploying with ports/arkweb/tools/deploy.py and running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_render.py on a device; a webview resize must repaint immediately rather than leaving the previous frame.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
